omaxian-session (1.2.0-1) excalibur; urgency=medium

  * New upstream Omaxian shell v1.2.0 (tag v1.2.0 = main @ 71125373, "Merge
    pull request #16"; fetch-omaxian.sh verifies the tag against the pinned
    commit). Vendors Omarchy v4.5.0.
  * The home template's community-apps now come from the binaries v1.2.0
    pins in community-apps/<app>/.omaxian-prebuilt (sha256-verified, via each
    app's own install.sh): disktree (tobi/disktree v0.11.0), omacalc, omacut,
    omarchy-meeting-recorder, omawrite, plain, signed (Omaxian release
    apps-93d0514). No local Rust or Qt builds for them any more.
  * Folio and Monologue are still built from source with Qt 6.8 compat
    patches: their apps-93d0514 binaries link on Qt 6.8 but the compiled-in
    QML uses Qt >= 6.9 properties (Flickable.acceptedButtons,
    VideoOutput.mirrored / endOfStreamPolicy) and fails to load. Folio's
    QDir::mkpath compat patch is dropped (upstreamed in v1.2.0).
  * Depends: libglib2.0-0t64 (Folio) and libturbojpeg0 (Monologue), newly
    listed in v1.2.0's omaxian.deps.json.

 -- Omaxian OS <dev@omaxian.org>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:45:48 +0100

omaxian-session (1.1.3-1) excalibur; urgency=medium

  * New upstream Omaxian shell v1.1.3 (tag v1.1.3 = main @ 2ffd66d8, "Merge
    pull request #13"; fetch-omaxian.sh verifies the tag against the pinned
    commit). Vendors Omarchy v4.5.0.
  * The home template seeds ALL nine community-apps: disktree, folio,
    monologue, omacalc, omacut, omarchy-meeting-recorder, omawrite, plain,
    signed (Qt 6.8 compat patches for folio and monologue in
    patches/community-apps/). community-plugins stay opt-in.
  * Depends: runtime packages of the new apps; xfce4-power-manager and xfconf
    (run by i3_autostart) move from Recommends to Depends; thunar dropped.
  * omaxian-default-file-manager (strata|folio, --system, --user, --login)
    and Xsession.d/26omaxian-defaults: apply the installer's file-manager
    choice and OnlyOffice titlebar=system at login, never over a user choice.
  * /etc/skel/.config/onlyoffice/DesktopEditors.conf ([General]
    titlebar=system); omaxian-seed-home merges INI files the installer
    already wrote instead of skipping them.

